From: Rémi Bernon <rbernon@codeweavers.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: Flush GL commands when activating another context.

Backport of WineHQ commit 1c144117a8 (wine-11.18), adapted. Upstream adds
the flush to macdrv_context_activate(), a function a later upstream
refactor split out of the base's macdrv_make_current(); upstream reaches
it both when another context is made current and when the thread releases
its context. The same line is placed at the start of
macdrv_make_current(), before the release path, while
NtCurrentTeb()->glReserved2 still holds the context being left, so both
cases flush. On the base this matters when a thread switches between
shared contexts or releases one before another thread samples what it
drew, and for the internal context wglBindTexImageARB pushes.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
index 2fd17ac..deb6d40 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
@@ -2304,6 +2304,8 @@ static BOOL macdrv_make_current(struct opengl_drawable *draw_base, struct opengl
 
     TRACE("draw %s, read %s, context %p\n", debugstr_opengl_drawable(draw_base), debugstr_opengl_drawable(read_base), private);
 
+    if (NtCurrentTeb()->glReserved2) funcs->p_glFlush();
+
     if (!private)
     {
         macdrv_make_context_current(NULL, NULL, CGRectNull);
